CORE thorough-smt-backend no-new-smt
many_pointers.c
--function f --object-bits 12
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[f.assertion.1\] line \d+ assertion 0: FAILURE$
--
^warning: ignoring
reached the limit of
--
There is no limit on the number of objects allocated for nondet inputs unless
--max-dynamic-object-instances is given, so the last pointer can be non-null.
The 1001 objects make the formula too large for the SMT back-ends: the
CPROVER SMT2 solver runs out of memory, and the incremental SMT2 back-end fails
an invariant ("=" applied to terms of different sorts).
